WEBVTT

NOTE Transcript of the narration

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.200
In 1666, an apple falls,
and a question begins.

2
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:07.770
Newton wrote it down.

3
00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:11.400
Force grows with mass and fades
with the square of distance.

4
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:17.800
In the orbit room, you launch planets
and watch his law hold them in place.

5
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.194
In 1962, Jan Tinbergen
swapped mass for economic size

6
00:00:24.194 --> 00:00:26.700
and let the data estimate distance.

7
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.300
Drag gamma and watch Vietnam's
trade with the world reroute.

8
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.355
For investment into Vietnam,
distance still matters:

9
00:00:38.355 --> 00:00:40.700
a coefficient of minus 0.38.

10
00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:42.955
Ask Lumina anything.

11
00:00:42.955 --> 00:00:47.600
Every answer comes from the references,
and every answer cites its source.

12
00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:53.100
No account, no tracking.
It all runs on your device.

13
00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:58.400
Gravity Lab: from Newton's
apple to FDI in Vietnam.
